#: src/routes/projects/ml/krasnal/+page.svelte
msgid "Krasnal is a chess engine developed in Wrocław, based on the Transformer architecture. It utilizes deep neural networks to learn to play chess intuitively, departing from traditional, heavy calculations and game tree searching."
msgstr "Krasnal is a chess engine developed in Wrocław, based on the Transformer architecture. It utilizes deep neural networks to learn to play chess intuitively, departing from traditional, heavy calculations and game tree searching."

#: src/routes/projects/ml/krasnal/+page.svelte
msgid "System architecture"
msgstr "System architecture"

#: src/routes/projects/ml/krasnal/+page.svelte
msgid "Investigating the model's behavior depending on the training method."
msgstr "Investigating the model's behavior depending on the training method."

#: src/routes/projects/ml/krasnal/+page.svelte
msgid "Training a model that generates legal and strong chess moves resembling human play."
msgstr "Training a model that generates legal and strong chess moves resembling human play."

#: src/routes/projects/ml/krasnal/+page.svelte
msgid "Krasnal's goal is to generate strong, yet human-like chess moves. Balancing between the intuition known from the Maia Chess project and the playing strength of Stockfish."
msgstr "Krasnal's goal is to generate strong, yet human-like chess moves. Balancing between the intuition known from the Maia Chess project and the playing strength of Stockfish."

#: src/routes/projects/ml/physarum/+page.svelte
msgid "Visualization of U-Matrix, Hit Map, and Weight Vectors"
msgstr "Visualization of U-Matrix, Hit Map, and Weight Vectors"

#: src/routes/projects/ml/physarum/+page.svelte
msgid "This project explores the fascinating intersection of biology and computer science, testing whether the natural processes of <0>Physarum polycephalum</0> can be used to perform computational tasks, such as training neural networks."
msgstr "This project explores the fascinating intersection of biology and computer science, testing whether the natural processes of <0>Physarum polycephalum</0> can be used to perform computational tasks, such as training neural networks."

#: src/routes/projects/ml/physarum/+page.svelte
msgid "Behavioral and experimental research on <0>Physarum polycephalum</0>."
msgstr "Behavioral and experimental research on <0>Physarum polycephalum</0>."

#: src/routes/projects/ml/physarum/+page.svelte
msgid "Algorithmic analysis and modeling of transport networks."
msgstr "Algorithmic analysis and modeling of transport networks."

#: src/routes/projects/ml/physarum/+page.svelte
msgid "Disseminating results within and beyond the academic community."
msgstr "Disseminating results within and beyond the academic community."

#: src/routes/projects/ket/+page.svelte
msgid "The KET project focuses on pure quantum algorithmics, moving computation modeling to a level of abstraction familiar from classical software engineering. It allows you to learn and run code on a real quantum processor without requiring advanced knowledge of physics, optics, or cryogenics. The development path leads from the basics of qubit operation and cryptography in the Qiskit environment, through complexity theory, to variational optimization methods. In the final phase, participants face the challenges of modern hardware, learning advanced error-correcting codes, magic state distillation, and Quantum Machine Learning."
msgstr "The KET project focuses on pure quantum algorithmics, moving computation modeling to a level of abstraction familiar from classical software engineering. It allows you to learn and run code on a real quantum processor without requiring advanced knowledge of physics, optics, or cryogenics. The development path leads from the basics of qubit operation and cryptography in the Qiskit environment, through complexity theory, to variational optimization methods. In the final phase, participants face the challenges of modern hardware, learning advanced error-correcting codes, magic state distillation, and Quantum Machine Learning."

#: src/routes/projects/ket/+page.svelte
msgid "Researching innovative quantum algorithms, computational complexity theory, and quantum machine learning to push the boundaries of modern cybersecurity and optimization paradigms."
msgstr "Researching innovative quantum algorithms, computational complexity theory, and quantum machine learning to push the boundaries of modern cybersecurity and optimization paradigms."

#: src/routes/projects/ket/+page.svelte
msgid "Modeling computations and independently implementing proprietary quantum algorithms in the Qiskit environment, with the ultimate execution of the code on a real quantum processor."
msgstr "Modeling computations and independently implementing proprietary quantum algorithms in the Qiskit environment, with the ultimate execution of the code on a real quantum processor."

